# onnxruntime-node (the home voice engine: kokoro-js → @huggingface/transformers → onnxruntime-node) downloads extra
# CUDA/GPU files from GitHub when it is installed on Linux x64. That download fails (404) and stops `npm ci` in
# Cloudflare's build (Linux). The app only uses the CPU files that ship inside the package, so skip it.
# Its install script reads this as npm_config_onnxruntime_node_install_cuda (npm 10 and 11 pass it on; npm prints
# "Unknown project config" — harmless). Windows never downloads anything, so the home computer is not affected.
onnxruntime-node-install-cuda=skip
